# Compiled bytecode must never reach the Skills API.
#
# scripts/deploy.ts zips each .claude/skills/<dir>/ whole, with no exclusions.
# A .pyc embeds the compiling machine's absolute source path in co_filename, so
# 14 of them were shipping paths like
#   /Users/bb/repos/claude-agent-starter/managed/.../validate_dossier.py
# and, in one case, the path to the founder's .env. Stale bytecode can also
# shadow an edited source file.
#
# This file stops them being committed. It does NOT stop the zip — that needs
# `-x "*__pycache__*" -x "*.pyc"` on the execFileSync call in scripts/deploy.ts,
# which is shared starter infrastructure and not ours to change.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Scratch output from local runs. Real fixtures live in fixtures/ and are
# committed; anything written by a run is reproducible and is not.
.cache/
*.log
